WEBVTT

NOTE Narration is displayed in the caption strip below the video by default.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.891
The supplied fictional case includes two reports: a customer lost unfinished answers on a phone, and a front-desk colleague explained unfamiliar wording.

00:00:09.891 --> 00:00:14.837
Label both reported and name the teaching case as the source.

00:00:14.837 --> 00:00:26.077
Now add three anticipated questions: can a customer correct the summary, can someone receive assisted intake, and who will have time for the added checking?

00:00:26.077 --> 00:00:28.775
These are possibilities, not invented feedback.

00:00:28.775 --> 00:00:32.821
That gives five realistic concerns with honest evidence labels.

00:00:32.821 --> 00:00:39.565
An AI claim that all customers prefer online intake has no supplied support; reject it.

00:00:39.565 --> 00:00:42.263
Correction authority needs a factual answer.

00:00:42.263 --> 00:00:44.960
Experience of added workload needs listening.

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:48.557
Resources for an assisted route need leadership approval.

00:00:48.557 --> 00:00:51.255
A concern can need several responses.

00:00:51.255 --> 00:00:55.301
Keep the question, evidence status and human owner together.
